###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The Mo run stands for an ensemble of five potentials; the errors are ensemble means and their 95% intervals are in the metric labels.
# - The Ag-Pd potential is 'the same potential as in Section 5.2' (level 16, cutoff 5 A, mindist 2 A, radial basis size 6); its DFT settings and the later, high-fidelity stage of the aluminium example were not read in full, so the Al run has no errors and no final training-set size.
# - The exchange-correlation functional is not named in the parts read for any of the three examples.
# - Property results (elastic constants of Mo in Table 2, the melting point of Al, the Ag-Pd convex hull) have no MetricProperty.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Training/reliability'; it is the MLIP software paper.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

